+
+Wasmer detects Next.js, installs dependencies with the pinned pnpm version, runs `pnpm run build` (`next build`) and serves the production build with Node. The button builds this public repo as-is and does not fork or copy it; to customize the template (start with `app/page.tsx` and `components/`) and redeploy on every push, fork it and connect your fork from the Wasmer dashboard. Set these in the app's Settings → Environment Vars:
+
+- `NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` (required): without it the home page returns a 500 error.
+- `CLERK_SECRET_KEY` (required): set it together with the publishable key, as in `.env.example`.
+- `GITHUB_OAUTH_TOKEN` (optional): authenticates the GitHub API request for the star count on the home page.
